[{:db/id 17592186110619 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c21712e7-21c4-5b84-b421-b21aa39ca232" "question-ea7a15b7-4301-5282-88af-359487b5befc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110320 :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{2x+5}{30} = \\dfrac{1}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+5}{30} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ (2x+5)\\cdot 2 & =30\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x+5)\\cdot 2 & =30\\cdot 1 \\\\ 4x+10 & =30 \\\\ 4x+10-10 & =30-10 \\\\ 4x & =20 \\\\ \\frac{4x}{4} & =\\frac{20}{4} \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110620 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-246474dc-65ca-5dbb-80ff-e29f8ffb3cb5" "question-80d602e5-e159-5437-af51-932d09f28858"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110321 :question/problem "Solve for $x$, where $\\dfrac{6-2x}{2} = \\dfrac{6-x}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6-2x}{2} & =\\frac{6-x}{3} \\\\ (6-2x)\\cdot 3 & =2\\cdot (6-x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6-2x)\\cdot 3 & =2\\cdot (6-x) \\\\ 18-6x & =12-2x \\\\ 18-6x-18 & =12-2x-18 \\\\ -6x & =-2x-6 \\\\ -6x+2x & =-2x-6+2x \\\\ -4x & =-6 \\\\ \\frac{-4x}{-4} & =\\frac{-6}{-4} \\\\ x & =\\frac{6}{4} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110621 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c11f4c73-9d61-5e53-addf-f63464a71f44" "question-bb61cd26-be58-5f6a-a7c8-fd462a5c81f3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110322 :question/problem "Solve for $u$, where $\\dfrac{u+2}{3} = - \\dfrac{3-u}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We transfer the negative into the numerator of the fraction, and proceed with cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{u+2}{3} & =-\\frac{3-u}{2} \\\\ \\frac{u+2}{3} & =\\frac{-(3-u)}{2} \\\\ \\frac{u+2}{3} & =\\frac{-3+u}{2} \\\\ (u+2)\\cdot 2 & =3\\cdot (-3+u)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u+2)\\cdot 2 & =3\\cdot (-3+u) \\\\ 2u+4 & =-9+3u \\\\ 2u+4-2u & =-9+3u-2u \\\\ 4 & =-9+u \\\\ 4+9 & =-9+u+9 \\\\ 13 & =u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=13.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-c21712e7-21c4-5b84-b421-b21aa39ca232" :question/id #uuid "c21712e7-21c4-5b84-b421-b21aa39ca232" :question/math-academy-id "q-44339" :question/problem "Solve for $k$ where $\\frac{9k-5}{6}=\\frac{k}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9k-5}{6} & =\\frac{k}{2} \\\\ (9k-5)\\cdot 2 & =6\\cdot k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9k-5)\\cdot 2 & =6\\cdot k \\\\ 18k-10 & =6k \\\\ 18k-10-18k & =6k-18k \\\\ -10 & =-12k \\\\ \\frac{-10}{-12} & =\\frac{-12k}{-12} \\\\ \\frac{10}{12} & =k \\\\ \\frac{5}{6} & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $k=\\frac{5}{6}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c54ab98f-d5bf-5d02-a021-f59b3a4bac35"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c54ab98f-d5bf-5d02-a021-f59b3a4bac35" :answer-field/id #uuid "c54ab98f-d5bf-5d02-a021-f59b3a4bac35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-63cf2218-3815-5dcc-88a1-3d42ae5f9b8c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-91eed268-75cf-5793-8477-90881d0f9173" "answer-6da8d60e-97ea-5928-b04b-cdbd9fcc3e85" "answer-1f3e710d-9fd5-5437-98b6-123729eb2da2" "answer-63cf2218-3815-5dcc-88a1-3d42ae5f9b8c" "answer-0a45ca0d-d65f-513c-9002-45aaa9adc8a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91eed268-75cf-5793-8477-90881d0f9173" :answer/id #uuid "91eed268-75cf-5793-8477-90881d0f9173" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "an