3fd389a5-7049-5019-81b0-f04bbd0ca8ce" :answer-field/choices ["answer-873bb01d-c51c-5a28-9714-1be8eb59e277" "answer-b93fb8d2-9112-5548-99a4-f156ce9be7ca" "answer-d702c1d2-8718-5e9f-b6a9-f8cec2dc39b8" "answer-3fd389a5-7049-5019-81b0-f04bbd0ca8ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-873bb01d-c51c-5a28-9714-1be8eb59e277" :answer/id #uuid "873bb01d-c51c-5a28-9714-1be8eb59e277" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "=+\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b93fb8d2-9112-5548-99a4-f156ce9be7ca" :answer/id #uuid "b93fb8d2-9112-5548-99a4-f156ce9be7ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "=-\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d702c1d2-8718-5e9f-b6a9-f8cec2dc39b8" :answer/id #uuid "d702c1d2-8718-5e9f-b6a9-f8cec2dc39b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fd389a5-7049-5019-81b0-f04bbd0ca8ce" :answer/id #uuid "3fd389a5-7049-5019-81b0-f04bbd0ca8ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "=\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d48b0cc5-05e8-55c3-b441-64611554a8ed" :question/id #uuid "d48b0cc5-05e8-55c3-b441-64611554a8ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-253553" :question/problem "Consider the set $B=[-1,2).$ Complete the following reasoning to identify $inf(B).$\n\nThe infimum of $B$ is the {{field-1}} of $B.$\n\nThe set of lower bounds of $B$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x{{field-2}}{{field-3}}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $B$ is the greatest lower bound of $B.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $B$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\le -1$ is smaller than or equal to the elements of $B.$ Thus, the set $(-\\infty ,-1]$ contains only lower bounds of $B.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x>-1$ is **not** a lower bound of $B.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $B$ that is smaller than $x$ for any $x>-1.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,-1]$ is the set of lower bounds of $B,$ and\n\n$$\ninf(B)=max(-\\infty ,-1]=-1.\n$$\n\nNotice that $-1$ is also the minimum of $B.$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe infimum of $B$ is the $\\text{greatest lower bound}$ of $B.$\n\nThe set of lower bounds of $B$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x\\le -1\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $inf(B)=-1\\in B.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7711e40c-c300-5c27-b9a0-b4edcb7004f6" "answer-field-020067a1-9263-50e4-b33c-092afcb490cd" "answer-field-8228ce6d-4eae-56db-adb9-39e0b92fe3e4" "answer-field-19e3672d-b2c0-5d72-8182-458842a8082b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7711e40c-c300-5c27-b9a0-b4edcb7004f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "7711e40c-c300-5c27-b9a0-b4edcb7004f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-c1157647-1f2f-5647-ba3c-a7d0af45f9e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c1157647-1f2f-5647-ba3c-a7d0af45f9e2" "answer-b3f10959-4573-5095-94c3-45484a99ec71" "answer-de33f900-f0ee-54b2-86e2-8e0dbacd4624" "answer-258f7939-f785-5dc4-a181-5aba44350878"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1157647-1f2f-5647-ba3c-a7d0af45f9e2" :answer/id #uuid "c1157647-1f2f-5647-ba3c-a7d0af45f9e2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "greatest lower bound" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3f10959-4573-5095-94c3-45484a99ec71" :answer/id #uuid "b3f10959-4573-5095-94c3-45484a99ec71" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "greatest upper bound" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de33f900-f0ee-54b2-86e2-8e0dbacd4624" :answer/id #uuid "de33f900-f0ee-54b2-86e2-8e0dbacd4624" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "smallest lower bound" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-258f7939-f785-5dc4-a181-5aba44350878" :a