wer-f201bf17-2033-520f-b0ef-29cc73c56264" :answer/id #uuid "f201bf17-2033-520f-b0ef-29cc73c56264" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2047cbfe-c2a1-5346-83bd-23d20199308f" :answer/id #uuid "2047cbfe-c2a1-5346-83bd-23d20199308f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a63c8a33-a6cd-5708-b3d4-76e8a627257a" :answer/id #uuid "a63c8a33-a6cd-5708-b3d4-76e8a627257a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c5891ca3-f381-532b-913f-b6dc3bcab055" :question/id #uuid "c5891ca3-f381-532b-913f-b6dc3bcab055" :question/math-academy-id "q-223145" :question/problem "If ${4}^{x}=\\frac{1}{4},$ then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $\\frac{1}{4}$ as ${4}^{-1}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{x} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {4}^{x} & ={4}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(4)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{x} & ={4}^{-1} \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fdd615eb-4925-5039-bbc3-b187bac64900"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fdd615eb-4925-5039-bbc3-b187bac64900" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdd615eb-4925-5039-bbc3-b187bac64900" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6fd3c8d2-c437-5775-8892-990be1d8c600" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6fd3c8d2-c437-5775-8892-990be1d8c600"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fd3c8d2-c437-5775-8892-990be1d8c600" :answer/id #uuid "6fd3c8d2-c437-5775-8892-990be1d8c600" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fa2ae142-bf31-5242-a307-d8faa66809d6" :question/id #uuid "fa2ae142-bf31-5242-a307-d8faa66809d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-223149" :question/problem "If ${6}^{t}=\\frac{1}{36},$ then $t=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $36$ as ${6}^{2}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{t} & =\\frac{1}{36} \\\\ {6}^{t} & =\\frac{1}{{6}^{2}} \\\\ {6}^{t} & ={6}^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(6)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{t} & ={6}^{-2} \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $t=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-61d05db5-0e4d-5d3d-9a30-6426013fad19"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-61d05db5-0e4d-5d3d-9a30-6426013fad19" :answer-field/id #uuid "61d05db5-0e4d-5d3d-9a30-6426013fad19" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b2e01ff2-d747-5b9e-b936-49bec7a790ee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b2e01ff2-d747-5b9e-b936-49bec7a790ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2e01ff2-d747-5b9e-b936-49bec7a790ee" :answer/id #uuid "b2e01ff2-d747-5b9e-b936-49bec7a790ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069158 :question/problem "If $2\\cdot {6}^{k}=72,$ then $k=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by dividing both sides by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot {6}^{k} & =72 \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot {6}^{k}}{2} & =\\frac{72}{2} \\\\ {6}^{k} & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite $36$ as ${6}^{2}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{k} & =36 \\\\ {6}^{k} & ={6}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(6)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{k} & ={6}^{2} \\\\ k & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186066202 :answer-field/correct "answer-bf7b7247-c19a-5409-86f4-f0606135b5c0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bf7b7247-c19a-5409-86f4-f0606135b5c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf7b7247-c19a-5409-86f4-f0606135b5c0" :answer/id #uuid "bf7b7247-c19a-5409-86f4-f0606135b5c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-936aa682-294b-52d5-96a5-a38d57d9bb85" :question/id #uuid "936aa682-294b-52d5-96a5-a38d57d9bb85" :question/math-academy-id "q-79" :question/problem "Solve the equation $3\\cdot {5}^{s}=75.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by dividing both sides by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot {5}^{s} & =75 \\\\ \\frac{3\\cdot {5}^{s}}{3} & =\\frac{75}{3} \\\\ {5}^{s} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite $25$ as ${5}^{2}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{s} & =25 \\\\ {5}^{s} & ={5}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(5)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{s} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ s & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $s=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b2849359-5d6c-5842-a26a-8a8a92947a85"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b2849359-5d6c-5842-a26a-8a8a92947a85" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2849359-5d6c-5842-a26a-8a8a92947a85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dcde4de5-148b-550d-8995-4b8efe5d538e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aef6b46e-f96f-53a7-8abb-2dd68d2f25aa" "answer-20f1cd8f-5953-547a-9323-05381b8876e4" "answer-57465c9d-f241-5b42-8c80-c0f976e0ace8" "answer-dcde4de5-148b-550d-8995-4b8efe5d538e" "answer-201fd078-e935-5796-b6c6-90bb35ee3d53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aef6b46e-f96f-53a7-8abb-2dd68d2f25aa" :answer/id #uuid "aef6b46e-f96f-53a7-8abb-2dd68d2f25aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20f1cd8f-5953-547a-9323-05381b8876e4" :answer/id #uuid "20f1cd8f-5953-547a-9323-05381b8876e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57465c9d-f241-5b42-8c80-c0f976e0ace8" :answer/id #uuid "57465c9d-f241-5b42-8c80-c0f976e0ace8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcde4de5-148b-550d-8995-4b8efe5d538e" :answer/id #uuid "dcde4de5-148b-550d-8995-4b8efe5d538e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-201fd078-e935-5796-b6c6-90bb35ee3d53" :answer/id #uuid "201fd078-e935-5796-b6c6-90bb35ee3d53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186070028 :tutorial/content "What is the value of $x$ that satisfies the following equation?\n\n$$\n3^x = 3^4\n$$\n\nWe call this an **exponential equation** because the variable is contained within the exponent. \n\nNow, this equation is pretty easy to solve. Because the bases on both sides of the equation are the same (they are both equal to $3$), we can simply equate the powers.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{x} & ={3}^{4} \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to this equation is $x=4.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186070029 :tutorial/content "Let's take a look at the following equation: \n\n$$\n5^x = 25\n$$\n\nWe can't solve this equation straight off the bat because the two sides of the equation don't share a common base.\n\nHowever, notice that $25$ can be written as a power of $5\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n25=5^2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite the equation as\n\n$$\n5^x = 5^2.\n$$\n\nSince both sides of the equation are now written as an exponential expression with a common base of $5,$ we can set the exponents equal to each other and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{x} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo check that the solution is correct, we plug $x=2$ into the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t5^{2} &= 25 \\\n\t\t25 &= 25 \\; {\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068938 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186080051 :answer-field/choices 17592186080052] [:db/retract 17592186080051 :answer-field/choices 17592186080053] [:db/retract 17592186080051 :answer-field/choices 17592186080054] [:db/retract 17592186080051 :answer-field/choices 17592186080055] [:db/retract 17592186080051 :answer-field/choices 17592186080056] {:db/id 17592186083180 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f18ce5af-43bd-5993-814d-ed1e89769ace" "question-0794aaff-8257-5ff5-95bd-c8b72d62b6ae"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083526 :question/problem "![](images/e0/e07a67e287b43cad2785d717393a3868803b94dffed14040fdf1329dd6bc9378.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the lowest and highest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The lowest $y$-value is $-1.$ This occurs at the point $(-4,-1).$\n\n- The highest $y$-value is $1.$ This occurs at the point $(4,1).$ However note that this point is not actually included in the graph.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-1$ and $1,$ including $-1$ but not including $1.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-1\\le y<1,$ which can also be written as  $-1\\le f(x)<1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186080051 :answer-field/correct "answer-f669d99f-f22f-5736-807c-f6a7b2de210d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f669d99f-f22f-5736-807c-f6a7b2de210d" "answer-15ccbd64-dd37-5c1c-ac0c-62783d6002f8" "answer-1f37bcb0-b9d9-5a12-8b71-9c9a950fd0a3" "answer-87a3ab71-ea35-509e-9e3f-5556d8497808" "answer-c4ba7457-4a29-535a-b0e5-20a84b3a0639"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f669d99f-f22f-5736-807c-f6a7b2de210d" :answer/id #uuid "f669d99f-f22f-5736-807c-f6a7b2de210d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\le f(x)<1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15ccbd64-dd37-5c1c-ac0c-62783d6002f8" :answer/id #uuid "15ccbd64-dd37-5c1c-ac0c-62783d6002f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\le f(x)\\le 0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f37bcb0-b9d9-5a12-8b71-9c9a950fd0a3" :answer/id #uuid "1f37bcb0-b9d9-5a12-8b71-9c9a950fd0a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\le f(x)\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87a3ab71-ea35-509e-9e3f-5556d8497808" :answer/id #uuid "87a3ab71-ea35-509e-9e3f-5556d8497808" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4<f(x)<4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4ba7457-4a29-535a-b0e5-20a84b3a0639" :answer/id #uuid "c4ba7457-4a29-535a-b0e5-20a84b3a0639" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\le f(x)\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083179 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c17be40c-81be-54ae-93a6-293eae7f05d7" "question-f6271452-0c9d-5cbb-808a-a03630c0e389"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c17be40c-81be-54ae-93a6-293eae7f05d7" :question/id #uuid "c17be40c-81be-54ae-93a6-293eae7f05d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-37027" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $h$ defined by the following table?\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $4$ | $-5$ | $6$ | $-7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $h(x)$ | $0$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $3$ | $-4$ | $5$ | $-6$ | $7$ |" :question/worked-solution "The range of $h(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a table, the range consists of all numbers that feature in the row corresponding to $h(x).$\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{-6,-4,-2,0,1,3,5,7\\}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5cc0bbc9-e32a-5c02-a5ea-63505b608b9c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5cc0bbc9-e32a-5c02-a5ea-63505b608b9c" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cc0bbc9-e32a-5c02-a5ea-63505b608b9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-78dd9aa6-9e83-5292-b186-73b2f4cc12de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a9c18ff8-03ed-5a26-9279-ad019db3f2bb" "answer-11dda732-4b38-5d2d-945d-43e23eb61bd5" "answer-78dd9aa6-9e83-5292-b186-73b2f4cc12de" "answer-ae4b3ee0-e0a4-547e-873b-10171c79bb3b" "answer-3ef48750-e872-55e8-879b-29227874153e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9c18ff8-03ed-5a26-9279-ad019db3f2bb" :answer/id #uuid "a9c18ff8-03ed-5a26-9279-ad019db3f2bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11dda732-4b38-5d2d-945d-43e23eb61bd5" :answer/id #uuid "11dda732-4b38-5d2d-945d-43e23eb61bd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-6,7]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78dd9aa6-9e83-5292-b186-73b2f4cc12de" :answer/id #uuid "78dd9aa6-9e83-5292-b186-73b2f4cc12de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-6,-4,-2,0,1,3,5,7\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae4b3ee0-e0a4-547e-873b-10171c79bb3b" :answer/id #uuid "ae4b3ee0-e0a4-547e-873b-10171c79bb3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-6,7\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ef48750-e872-55e8-879b-29227874153e" :answer/id #uuid "3ef48750-e872-55e8-879b-29227874153e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0,7\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f6271452-0c9d-5cbb-808a-a03630c0e389" :question/id #uuid "f6271452-0c9d-5cbb-808a-a03630c0e389" :question/math-academy-id "q-79266" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f$ defined by the following table?\n\n| $x$ | $6$ | $7$ | $9$ | $11$ | $13$ | $14$ | $18$ | $19$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $5$ | $0$ | $8$ | $-10$ | $11$ | $-10$ | $5$ | $0$ |" :question/worked-solution "The range of $f(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a table, the range consists of all numbers that feature in the row corresponding to $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{-10,0,5,8,11\\}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fdbf69e7-910a-5185-95d7-1b30300b0a57"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fdbf69e7-910a-5185-95d7-1b30300b0a57" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdbf69e7-910a-5185-95d7-1b30300b0a57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c8327966-1579-50f4-8769-4f4b1d20b937" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e848015c-8529-5e20-997f-452f870dbae1" "answer-d6c9b848-eb9c-5da4-a5f0-aafd698f9eb5" "answer-c8327966-1579-50f4-8769-4f4b1d20b937" "answer-b53980ec-b15d-549a-8525-7a63afb3b2f3" "answer-f2190b72-89e7-54d5-927a-57b95863b4f6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e848015c-8529-5e20-997f-452f870dbae1" :answer/id #uuid "e848015c-8529-5e20-997f-452f870dbae1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,8)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6c9b848-eb9c-5da4-a5f0-aafd698f9eb5" :answer/id #uuid "d6c9b848-eb9c-5da4-a5f0-aafd698f9eb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-10,11]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8327966-1579-50f4-8769-4f4b1d20b937" :answer/id #uuid "c8327966-1579-50f4-8769-4f4b1d20b937" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-10,0,5,8,11\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b53980ec-b15d-549a-8525-7a63afb3b2f3" :answer/id #uuid "b53980ec-b15d-549a-8525-7a63afb3b2f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-10,11\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2190b72-89e7-54d5-927a-57b95863b4f6" :answer/id #uuid "f2190b72-89e7-54d5-927a-57b95863b4f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0,5,8,11\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f18ce5af-43bd-5993-814d-ed1e89769ace" :question/id #uuid "f18ce5af-43bd-5993-814d-ed1e89769ace" :question/math-academy-id "q-129337" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d94225e60a13742a70558cea252d7bffde2bab51bcb6942be510e7bbde6323e5.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the lowest and highest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The lowest $y$-value is $0.$ This occurs at the point $(4,0).$ However, note that this point is not actually included in the graph.\n\n- The highest $y$-value is $3.$ This occurs at the point $(-2,3).$ However, note that this point is not actually included in the graph.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $0$ and $3,$ but not including $0$ nor $3.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $0<y<3,$ which can also be written as  $0<f(x)<3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76d58179-406b-5f6d-bfb2-2743c8e8bdc1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76d58179-406b-5f6d-bfb2-2743c8e8bdc1" :answer-field/id #uuid "76d58179-406b-5f6d-bfb2-2743c8e8bdc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-10b99c2c-7707-5d66-8da2-a5686ff27235" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5eedf984-c57c-5a23-b01d-25c70190b6f8" "answer-11f89eee-1bbb-58b3-8fa4-b20195b0fc5d" "answer-5e18da27-97d3-5495-b1f2-041cf7e3c7bd" "answer-10b99c2c-7707-5d66-8da2-a5686ff27235" "answer-b30149ca-0055-5673-9eab-08614a1566db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5eedf984-c57c-5a23-b01d-25c70190b6f8" :answer/id #uuid "5eedf984-c57c-5a23-b01d-25c70190b6f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1<f(x)<3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11f89eee-1bbb-58b3-8fa4-b20195b0fc5d" :answer/id #uuid "11f89eee-1bbb-58b3-8fa4-b20195b0fc5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2<f(x)<4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e18da27-97d