d{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3ea4c1f3-b047-5bb2-9c1e-8cac1866a24f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3ea4c1f3-b047-5bb2-9c1e-8cac1866a24f" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ea4c1f3-b047-5bb2-9c1e-8cac1866a24f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3078ef9f-3489-5d8b-ae21-bed9d438ebc8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3ce7cc25-db51-5ab8-ad16-e86c21738942" "answer-3fe84686-85aa-5976-996a-2fa1720ef35b" "answer-3078ef9f-3489-5d8b-ae21-bed9d438ebc8" "answer-a027c945-ae2b-5b22-9676-fa021430c4c3" "answer-a2222c51-7aab-5c3a-97fa-f2cd7ac0df0d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ce7cc25-db51-5ab8-ad16-e86c21738942" :answer/id #uuid "3ce7cc25-db51-5ab8-ad16-e86c21738942" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fe84686-85aa-5976-996a-2fa1720ef35b" :answer/id #uuid "3fe84686-85aa-5976-996a-2fa1720ef35b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3078ef9f-3489-5d8b-ae21-bed9d438ebc8" :answer/id #uuid "3078ef9f-3489-5d8b-ae21-bed9d438ebc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a027c945-ae2b-5b22-9676-fa021430c4c3" :answer/id #uuid "a027c945-ae2b-5b22-9676-fa021430c4c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2222c51-7aab-5c3a-97fa-f2cd7ac0df0d" :answer/id #uuid "a2222c51-7aab-5c3a-97fa-f2cd7ac0df0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f6033ad1-0d99-515b-be18-2f73585eb731" :question/id #uuid "f6033ad1-0d99-515b-be18-2f73585eb731" :question/math-academy-id "q-218659" :question/problem "Given that $h(t)=5\\cdot {4}^{3t+6},$ find $t$ such that $h(t)=320.$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $h(t)=320$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n5\\cdot {4}^{3t+6}=320\n$$\n\nWe can divide both sides of the equation by the constant factor of $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5\\cdot {4}^{3t+6}}{5} & =\\frac{320}{5} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{5}\\cdot {4}^{3t+6}}{\\cancel{5}} & =64 \\\\ {4}^{3t+6} & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $t$ using the fact that $64$ is a power of $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{3t+6} & ={4}^{3} \\\\ 3t+6 & =3 \\\\ 3t & =-3 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aaa84f9b-eb74-5ae9-9fee-178d468d3d0a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aaa84f9b-eb74-5ae9-9fee-178d468d3d0a" :answer-field/id #uuid "aaa84f9b-eb74-5ae9-9fee-178d468d3d0a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-649ad70b-e688-5d26-97db-4e5143cbf659" :answer-field/choices ["answer-649ad70b-e688-5d26-97db-4e5143cbf659"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-649ad70b-e688-5d26-97db-4e5143cbf659" :answer/id #uuid "649ad70b-e688-5d26-97db-4e5143cbf659" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097924 :tutorial/content "An **exponential function** is a function where a variable is contained within an exponent. For example, the function below is an exponential function:\n\n$$\nf(x) = 3^x\n$$\n\nJust like any other function, we can evaluate it for some particular value of $x,$ say at $x={\\color{blue}{4}},$ by substituting this value of $x$ into the function:\n\n$$\nf(4) = 3^{\\color{blue}{4}} = 81\n$$\n\nAnother example of an exponential function is $g(x)$ below:\n\n$$\ng(x) = 16\\cdot \\left(\\dfrac 1 2\\right)^x\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this function at $x={\\color{blue}{4}}$ using the power of quotient rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(4) & =16\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{4} \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{{1}^{4}}{{2}^{4}} \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{1}{16} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExponential functions are of huge practical importance in science, engineering, economics, and many other disciplines. Let's practice evaluating them." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097925 :tutorial/content "Suppose that we're given the following exponential function:\n\n$$\nf(t) = C\\cdot 4^t\n$$\n\nIn addition, we're told that $f(3) = 128.$ Can we use this information to find the unknown constant $C?$\n\nTo solve this problem, we substitute $t=3$ and $f(t) = 128$ and solve for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}128 & =C\\cdot {4}^{3} \\\\ 128 & =C\\cdot 64 \\\\ \\frac{128}{64} & =C \\\\ 2 & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $C=2.$ So our function expressed in full is\n\n$$\nf(t) = 2\\cdot 4^t.\n$$\n\nWe sometimes say that the **initial value** of the function is $2,$ because if we evaluate $f$ at $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\nf(0) = 2\\cdot 4^0 = 2\\cdot 1 = 2.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097926 :tutorial/content "Let's consider the following exponential function:\n\n$$\nh(x) = 2^x\n$$\n\nCan we find the value of $x$ that gives $h(x)=64?$ Indeed, we can. To do this, we'll need to use our knowledge of exponential equations. \n\nFirst, we use the fact that $h(x)=64$ to write our equation as\n\n$$\n2^x = 64.\n$$\n\nThis is an exponential equation. Since we know that $64$ is a power of $2,$ we can solve this equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{x} & =64 \\\\ {2}^{x} & ={2}^{6} \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096918 :activity/expected-seconds 540.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186284360 :answer-field/choices 17592186282900] [:db/retract 17592186284360 :answer-field/choices 17592186282904] [:db/retract 17592186284360 :answer-field/choices 17592186281769] [:db/retract 17592186284360 :answer-field/choices 17592186281916] [:db/retract 17592186283953 :answer-field/choices 17592186282327] [:db/retract 17592186283953 :answer-field/choices 17592186282456] [:db/retract 17592186283953 :answer-field/choices 17592186283545] [:db/retract 17592186283953 :answer-field/choices 17592186282940] {:db/id 17592186124555 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cfd858a6-a00f-5a94-8347-c41608b62519"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124503 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-756c31bd-d0b5-518e-8fa8-bf3e64b797d5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284360 :answer-field/choices ["answer-a77b95d1-fceb-5a52-bb2a-611c7c686bdc" "answer-d3c48da9-56f6-56f4-b48e-a9ee4cfebf84" "answer-e4f233b9-83c6-5d23-a7ab-9cd273335e98" "answer-3dcc081f-8c87-52c8-b3e1-e3a8a332e58f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a77b95d1-fceb-5a52-bb2a-611c7c686bdc" :answer/id #uuid "a77b95d1-fceb-5a52-bb2a-611c7c686bdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}<1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3c48da9-56f6-56f4-b48e-a9ee4cfebf84" :answer/id #uuid "d3c48da9-56f6-56f4-b48e-a9ee4cfebf84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}>1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4f233b9-83c6-5d23-a7ab-9cd273335e98" :answer/id #uuid "e4f233b9-83c6-5d23-a7ab-9cd273335e98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}\\ge 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3dcc081f-8c87-52c8-b3e1-e3a8a332e58f" :answer/id #uuid "3dcc081f-8c87-52c8-b3e1-e3a8a332e58f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}\\le 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-756c31bd-d0b5-518e-8fa8-bf3e64b797d5" :question/id #uuid "756c31bd-d0b5-518e-8fa8-bf3e64b797d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-164306" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}-\\frac{(z+5)^{2}}{16}=-1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}-\\frac{(z+5)^{2}}{16} & =-1 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+1 & =\\frac{(z+5)^{2}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(z+5)^{2}}{16} & =(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+1 \\\\ (z+5)^{2} & =16((x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+1) \\\\ z+5 & =\\pm 4\\sqrt{(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+1} \\\\ z & =-5\\pm 4\\sqrt{(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+1\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-751f8b2e-9f8a-59f7-8b55-6cf5ae31cd83"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-751f8b2e-9f8a-59f7-8b55-6cf5ae31cd83" :answer-field/id #uuid "751f8b2e-9f8a-59f7-8b55-6cf5ae31cd83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3fcdf940-6360-5efc-815a-67685f2bcd39" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c13ff75f-ea2e-5e78-b3fd-6dfe315f448e" "answer-ad54fb20-d344-5be0-b621-c08138a7d222" "answer-c00ed966-6006-5b17-8212-cacd1e467d5b" "answer-8d2dd945-a79f-5959-bfa8-cdfafd1ac3cd" "answer-3fcdf940-6360-5efc-815a-67685f2bcd39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c13ff75f-ea2e-5e78-b3fd-6dfe315f448e" :answer/id #uuid "c13ff75f-ea2e-5e78-b3fd-6dfe315f448e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}<1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad54fb20-d344-5be0-b621-c08138a7d222" :answer/id #uuid "ad54fb20-d344-5be0-b621-c08138a7d222" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}>1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c00ed966-6006-5b17-8212-cacd1e467d5b" :answer/id #uuid "c00ed966-6006-5b17-8212-cacd1e467d5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}\\ge 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d2dd945-a79f-5959-bfa8-cdfafd1ac3cd" :answer/id #uuid "8d2dd945-a79f-5959-bfa8-cdfafd1ac3cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}\\le 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fcdf940-6360-5efc-815a-67685f2bcd39" :answer/id #uuid "3fcdf940-6360-5efc-815a-67685f2bcd39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284469 :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-(z-3)^{2} & =1 \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1 & =(z-3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z-3)^{2} & =(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1 \\\\ z-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} \\\\ z & =3\\pm \\sqrt{(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}-1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2} & \\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the exterior of the circle $(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ which includes the boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186283953 :answer-field/correct "answer-639e7663-1b18-512b-aaa1-be4700f6151a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c59c6bc5-e7d5-524f-b87d-e788fbdad7bc" "answer-389cbac5-a671-5c39-a922-51617d9c06fe" "answer-639e7663-1b18-512b-aaa1-be4700f6151a" "answer-36789465-716b-57b5-bcb5-c61d70e72a4f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c59c6bc5-e7d5-524f-b87d-e788fbdad7bc" :answer/id #uuid "c59c6bc5-e7d5-524f-b87d-e788fbdad7bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}<3\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-389cbac5-a671-5c39-a922-51617d9c06fe" :answer/id #uuid "389cbac5-a671-5c39-a922-51617d9c06fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}>1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-639e7663-1b18-512b-aaa1-be4700f6151a" :answer/id #uuid "639e7663-1b18-512b-aaa1-be4700f6151a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36789465-716b-57b5-bcb5-c61d70e72a4f" :answer/id #uuid "36789465-716b-57b5-bcb5-c61d70e72a4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 3\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cfd858a6-a00f-5a94-8347-c41608b62519" :question/id #uuid "cfd858a6-a00f-5a94-8347-c41608b62519" :question/math-academy-id "q-164375" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the hyperboloid of two sheets $-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=-1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperboloid. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{0}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-{z}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is the equation of a hyperbola in $xz$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eb913cd1-fa9a-53a5-80ea-84008e65ffbc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eb913cd1-fa9a-53a5-80ea-84008e65ffbc" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb913cd1-fa9a-53a5-80ea-84008e65ffbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cd8afb28-1c32-5f0f-a8c4-af9d56f35d12" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9f47998e-e870-56c4-baa4-8f352b659234" "answer-ecef13cd-61bd-588f-a9df-6b1c14e317f4" "answer-cd8afb28-1c32-5f0f-a8c4-af9d56f35d12" "answer-58602c0f-accf-5f29-9ed8-3bc7fca41325" "answer-a290ce1e-061b-5f18-9739-ce332aa415a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f47998e-e870-56c4-baa4-8f352b659234" :answer/id #uuid "9f47998e-e870-56c4-baa4-8f352b659234" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{z}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ecef13cd-61bd-588f-a9df-6b1c14e317f4" :answer/id #uuid "ecef13cd-61bd-588f-a9df-6b1c14e317f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-{y}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd8afb28-1c32-5f0f-a8c4-af9d56f35d12" :answer/id #uuid "cd8afb28-1c32-5f0f-a8c4-af9d56f35d12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-{z}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58602c0f-accf-5f29-9ed8-3bc7fca41325" :answer/id #uuid "58602c0f-accf-5f29-9ed8-3bc7fca41325" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a290ce1e-061b-5f18-9739-ce332aa415a3" :answer/id #uuid "a290ce1e-061b-5f18-9739-ce332aa415a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{z}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-f044953d-ed45-518b-a59c-617113ac03a7" :activity/id #uuid "f044953d-ed45-518b-a59c-617113ac03a7" :activity/title "Hyperboloids" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048527 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-fa19a58c-a70e-5db0-ade4-effabe26c294" "step-c766094c-6eab-58b2-b2f3-4c23eb53e41f" "step-e921225c-624b-5c95-9668-3ca7e3b9bedb" "step-346ce6bc-5f2c-5170-a37c-8daa10ff6d75" "step-ee6f7b73-925c-51b7-8db4-73cd3744c6e3"] :activity/first-step "step-fa19a58c-a70e-5db0-ade4-effabe26c294" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-fa19a58c-a70e-5db0-ade4-effabe26c294" :step/id #uuid "fa19a58c-a70e-5db0-ade4-effabe26c294" :step/content 17592186391951 :step/next "step-c766094c-6eab-58b2-b2f3-4c23eb53e41f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c766094c-6eab-58b2-b2f3-4c23eb53e41f" :step/id #uuid "c766094c-6eab-58b2-b2f3-4c23eb53e41f" :step/content 17592186284468 :step/next "step-e921225c-624b-5c95-9668-3ca7e3b9bedb" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e921225c-624b-5c95-9668-3ca7e3b9bedb" :step/id #uuid "e921225c-624b-5c95-9668-3ca7e3b9bedb" :step/content "question-756c31bd-d0b5-518e-8fa8-bf3e64b797d5" :step/next "step-346ce6bc-5f2c-5170-a37c-8daa10ff6d75" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-346ce6bc-5f2c-5170-a37c-8daa10ff6d75" :step/id #uuid "346ce6bc-5f2c-5170-a37c-8daa10ff6d75" :step/content 17592186284469 :step/next "step-ee6f7b73-925c-51b7-8db4-73cd3744c6e3" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ee6f7b73-925c-51b7-8db4-73cd3744c6e3" :step/id #uuid "ee6f7b73-925c-51b7-8db4-73cd3744c6e3" :step/content "question-cfd858a6-a00f-5a94-8347-c41608b62519" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166735 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fef70086-7b53-5958-83a3-40bb6490de70" "question-e7faa58d-c8b1-553c-876f-43b3b6090485" "question-06c6c230-3fa4-5b71-a2c3-1d7beda8e3c7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166498 :question/problem "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\textrm{Po}(9).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing value in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.1157\\,$ | $\\,0.2068\\,$ | $\\,0.3239\\,$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,?\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$ | $\\,0.5874\\,$ | $\\,0.7060\\,$ | $\\,0.8030\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\textrm{Po}(\\lambda)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{\\lambda^x e^{-\\lambda}}{x!}, \\qquad x=0,1,2,3, \\ldots\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda=9.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing element of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(8) & =P(X\\le 8) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 7)+P(X=8) \\\\  & =F(7)+P(X=8) \\\\  & =0.3239+\\frac{{9}^{8}\\cdot {e}^{-9}}{8!} \\\\  & ≈0.4557\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166736 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-47d084d0-558c-55b5-8190-75e291aec240" "question-77a09fd4-a75e-503e-85e7-5369cc0e38f9" "question-88a38ed6-7fa9-5b5b-87c9-ffc4db1074d1" "question-6ed46a6a-33c2-5d2f-895f-2046417a88d9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166499 :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X \\sim \\textrm{Po}(6)$ given below, compute $P(X=7).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0620\\,$ | $\\,0.1512\\,$ | $\\,0.2851\\,$ | $\\,0.4457\\,$ | $\\,0.6063\\,$ | $\\,0.7440\\,$ | $\\,0.8472\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & =P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\})+P(X=7) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 6)+P(X=7) \\\\  & =F(6)+P(X=7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=7) & =F(7)-F(6) \\\\  & =0.7440-0.6063 \\\\  & =0.1377.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166737 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bfd17aa5-30fb-5cb9-aef8-99d3d322cf8d" "question-a9431e7c-b663-534c-b1f2-e2cde30992c6" "question-d0dd1d6e-e305-5637-930e-c61c5f8b750e" "question-f97c8702-16dc-518f-875a-9b5c78750b8c" "question-3fd62c03-4c13-5eaa-a871-a2d0ae21b2c3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166500 :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X \\sim \\textrm{Po}(8)$ given below, compute $P(3 \\leq X \\leq 6).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0138\\,$ | $\\,0.0424\\,$ | $\\,0.0996\\,$ | $\\,0.1912\\,$ | $\\,0.3134\\,$ | $\\,0.4530\\,$ | $\\,0.5925\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(3\\le X\\le 6) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(3\\le X\\le 6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 6) & =F(6)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.3134-0.0138 \\\\  & =0.2996.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166738 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-51b5f656-5014-5979-a4cf-5d15629f454f" "question-9ba81e5b-3639-5408-81fe-d49741329753" "question-fcbdd763-0262-5c2f-847d-f89b9e62dad1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166501 :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X \\sim \\textrm{Po}(7)$ given below, compute $P(X \\geq 5).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0009\\,$ | $\\,0.0073\\,$ | $\\,0.0296\\,$ | $\\,0.0818\\,$ | $\\,0.1730\\,$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X > a) = 1 - P(X\\leq a) = 1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X \\geq 5) = P(X \\gt 4).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 5) & =P(X>4) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-F(4) \\\\  & =1-0.1730 \\\\  & =0.8270.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-fef70086-7b53-5958-83a3-40bb6490de70" :question/id #uuid "fef70086-7b53-5958-83a3-40bb6490de70" :question/math-academy-id "q-224988" :question/problem "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(7).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing values in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $\\,0.0296\\,$ | $\\,0.0818\\,$ | $\\,0.1730\\,$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =7.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{7}^{0}{e}^{-7}}{0!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0009\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{7}^{0}\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{0!}+\\frac{{7}^{1}\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{1}+\\frac{7\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0073\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-04f5f413-0f98-5505-983e-d59a63258e11" "answer-field-9c72a0ab-81d8-5720-a0ce-49a7974bca0d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-04f5f413-0f98-5505-983e-d59a63258e11" :answer-field/id #uuid "04f5f413-0f98-5505-983e-d59a63258e11" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3cf46e97-2c49-5dc4-9720-738d9fcbf422" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3cf46e97-2c49-5dc4-9720-738d9fcbf422"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cf46e97-2c49-5dc4-9720-738d9fcbf422" :answer/id #uuid "3cf46e97-2c49-5dc4-9720-738d9fcbf422" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0009" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9c72a0ab-81d8-5720-a0ce-49a7974bca0d" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c72a0ab-81d8-5720-a0ce-49a7974bca0d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d1424711-bfed-5b96-95b9-807b329960d1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d1424711-bfed-5b96-95b9-807b329960d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1424711-bfed-5b96-95b9-807b329960d1" :answer/id #uuid "d1424711-bfed-5b96-95b9-807b329960d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0073" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167148 :question/problem "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(5).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing values in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $\\,0.1247\\,$ | $\\,0.2650\\,$ | $\\,0.4405\\,$ | $\\,0.6160\\,$ | $\\,0.7622\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =5.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{0}{e}^{-5}}{0!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-5}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0067.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{0}\\cdot {e}^{-5}}{0!}+\\frac{{5}^{1}\\cdot {e}^{-5}}{1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-5}}{1}+\\frac{5\\cdot {e}^{-5}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0404.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163952 :answer-field/correct "answer-06a0bcc3-d25c-57e6-b83c-d86187510afa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06a0bcc3-d25c-57e6-b83c-d86187510afa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06a0bcc3-d25c-57e6-b83c-d86187510afa" :answer/id #uuid "06a0bcc3-d25c-57e6-b83c-d86187510afa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0067" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163953 :answer-field/correct "answer-1c67ea15-0a12-572c-9654-5f17c706ecfd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1c67ea15-0a12-572c-9654-5f17c706ecfd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c67ea15-0a12-572c-9654-5f17c706ecfd" :answer/id #uuid "1c67ea15-0a12-572c-9654-5f17c706ecfd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0404" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e7faa58d-c8b1-553c-876f-43b3b6090485" :question/id #uuid "e7faa58d-c8b1-553c-876f-43b3b6090485" :question/math-academy-id "q-224984" :question/problem "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(6).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing values in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $\\,0.0620\\,$ | $\\,0.1512\\,$ | $\\,0.2851\\,$ | $\\,0.4457\\,$ | $\\,0.6063\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =6.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{0}{e}^{-6}}{0!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0025\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{0}\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{0!}+\\frac{{6}^{1}\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{1}+\\frac{6\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0174\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d2715bda-0578-54f8-a6f8-d5f30a7d8e25" "answer-field-2b8adfb2-b2e2-5e9c-ae22-d60ba87a03a5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d2715bda-0578-54f8-a6f8-d5f30a7d8e25" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2715bda-0578-54f8-a6f8-d5f30a7d8e25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9b6d52ea-41c1-5b97-a72e-2af5e66233c1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9b6d52ea-41c1-5b97-a72e-2af5e66233c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b6d52ea-41c1-5b97-a72e-2af5e66233c1" :answer/id #uuid "9b6d52ea-41c1-5b97-a72e-2af5e66233c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0025" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2b8adfb2-b2e2-5e9c-ae22-d60ba87a03a5" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b8adfb2-b2e2-5e9c-ae22-d60ba87a03a5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-13ae6705-d6fa-5a1b-a345-6039c632303a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-13ae6705-d6fa-5a1b-a345-6039c632303a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13ae6705-d6fa-5a1b-a345-6039c632303a" :answer/id #uuid "13ae6705-d6fa-5a1b-a345-6039c632303a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0174" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-06c6c230-3fa4-5b71-a2c3-1d7beda8e3c7" :question/id #uuid "06c6c230-3fa4-5b71-a2c3-1d7beda8e3c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-224989" :question/problem "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(12).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing value in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0203\\,$ | $\\,0.0458\\,$ | $\\,0.0895\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $\\,0.2424\\,$ | $\\,0.3472\\,$ | $\\,0.4616\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =12.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing element of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(8) & =P(X\\le 8) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 7)+P(X=8) \\\\  & =F(7)+P(X=8) \\\\  & =0.0895+\\frac{{12}^{8}\\cdot {e}^{-12}}{8!} \\\\  & ≈0.1550\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76d83c0e-8572-5ffe-a152-9df51921452d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76d83c0e-8572-5ffe-a152-9df51921452d" :answer-field/id #uuid "76d83c0e-8572-5ffe-a152-9df51921452d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5542ee15-2183-5eb0-9267-aae1b75ac496" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5542ee15-2183-5eb0-9267-aae1b75ac496"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5542ee15-2183-5eb0-9267-aae1b75ac496" :answer/id #uuid "5542ee15-2183-5eb0-9267-aae1b75ac496" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1550" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167149 :question/problem "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(7).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing value in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.1730\\,$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ | $\\,0.5987\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $\\,0.9015\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =7.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing element of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(9) & =P(X\\le 9) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 8)+P(X=9) \\\\  & =F(8)+P(X=9) \\\\  & =0.7291+\\frac{{7}^{9}\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{9!} \\\\  & ≈0.8305.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163954 :answer-field/correct "answer-3202583d-4b37-5bc6-9d6b-3f1926089c3a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3202583d-4b37-5bc6-9d6b-3f1926089c3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3202583d-4b37-5bc6-9d6b-3f1926089c3a" :answer/id #uuid "3202583d-4b37-5bc6-9d6b-3f1926089c3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8305" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-47d084d0-558c-55b5-8190-75e291aec240" :question/id #uuid "47d084d0-558c-55b5-8190-75e291aec240" :question/math-academy-id "q-224999" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(5)$ given below, compute $P(X<7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.2650\\,$ | $\\,0.4405\\,$ | $\\,0.6160\\,$ | $\\,0.7622\\,$ | $\\,0.8666\\,$ | $\\,0.9319\\,$ | $\\,0.9682\\,$ |\n\n$P(X<7)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<7) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =F(6) \\\\  & =0.7622.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8b252531-9953-5c30-bea3-fc9fef82d0df"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8b252531-9953-5c30-bea3-fc9fef82d0df" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b252531-9953-5c30-bea3-fc9fef82d0df" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8bb640e7-0a11-5457-b2f5-9e615281af0a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8bb640e7-0a11-5457-b2f5-9e615281af0a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bb640e7-0a11-5457-b2f5-9e615281af0a" :answer/id #uuid "8bb640e7-0a11-5457-b2f5-9e615281af0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7622" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-77a09fd4-a75e-503e-85e7-5369cc0e38f9" :question/id #uuid "77a09fd4-a75e-503e-85e7-5369cc0e38f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-224998" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(12)$ given below, compute $P(X<11).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $13$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0895\\,$ | $\\,0.1550\\,$ | $\\,0.2424\\,$ | $\\,0.3472\\,$ | $\\,0.4616\\,$ | $\\,0.5760\\,$ | $\\,0.6815\\,$ |\n\n$P(X<11)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<11) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,10\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 10) \\\\  & =F(10) \\\\  & =0.3472.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-93c362b2-2bb8-51e2-be3b-426a0b40223d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-93c362b2-2bb8-51e2-be3b-426a0b40223d" :answer-field/id #uuid "93c362b2-2bb8-51e2-be3b-426a0b40223d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5829e646-b58a-5440-a9ba-2533382195ba" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5829e646-b58a-5440-a9ba-2533382195ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5829e646-b58a-5440-a9ba-2533382195ba" :answer/id #uuid "5829e646-b58a-5440-a9ba-2533382195ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3472" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167150 :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(5)$ given below, find the value of $P(X\\le 6).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.1247\\,$ | $\\,0.2650\\,$ | $\\,0.4405\\,$ | $\\,0.6160\\,$ | $\\,0.7622\\,$ | $\\,0.8666\\,$ | $\\,0.9319\\,$ |\n\n$P(X\\le 6)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 6) & =F(6) \\\\  & =0.7622.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163955 :answer-field/correct "answer-2025cdb9-701f-5a0e-a302-0d874be139c8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2025cdb9-701f-5a0e-a302-0d874be139c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2025cdb9-701f-5a0e-a302-0d874be139c8" :answer/id #uuid "2025cdb9-701f-5a0e-a302-0d874be139c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7622" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-88a38ed6-7fa9-5b5b-87c9-ffc4db1074d1" :question/id #uuid "88a38ed6-7fa9-5b5b-87c9-ffc4db1074d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-224482" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(8)$ given below, compute $P(X=5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0424\\,$ | $\\,0.0996\\,$ | $\\,0.1912\\,$ | $\\,0.3134\\,$ | $\\,0.4530\\,$ | $\\,0.5925\\,$ | $\\,0.7166\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,4\\})+P(X=5) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(X=5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =F(5)-F(4) \\\\  & =0.1912-0.0996 \\\\  & =0.0916.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-696faedc-2423-51c5-9692-5e7bf27716e8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-696faedc-2423-51c5-9692-5e7bf27716e8" :answer-field/id #uuid "696faedc-2423-51c5-9692-5e7bf27716e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7dcf728f-a47d-5e95-aed1-0b2772b763e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8092ef73-0575-5ffe-914c-404ebb71f54a" "answer-7dcf728f-a47d-5e95-aed1-0b2772b763e2" "answer-724641d5-f288-51a5-8b41-9841bd8281cb" "answer-a9976404-9788-5cfd-942d-efed478db702" "answer-9862d14e-fa7e-5fe8-862b-20d65e72510b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8092ef73-0575-5ffe-914c-404ebb71f54a" :answer/id #uuid "8092ef73-0575-5ffe-914c-404ebb71f54a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0845" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dcf728f-a47d-5e95-aed1-0b2772b763e2" :answer/id #uuid "7dcf728f-a47d-5e95-aed1-0b2772b763e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0916" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-724641d5-f288-51a5-8b41-9841bd8281cb" :answer/id #uuid "724641d5-f288-51a5-8b41-9841bd8281cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0996" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9976404-9788-5cfd-942d-efed478db702" :answer/id #uuid "a9976404-9788-5cfd-942d-efed478db702" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1222" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9862d14e-fa7e-5fe8-862b-20d65e72510b" :answer/id #uuid "9862d14e-fa7e-5fe8-862b-20d65e72510b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3134" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6ed46a6a-33c2-5d2f-895f-2046417a88d9" :question/id #uuid "6ed46a6a-33c2-5d2f-895f-2046417a88d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-225004" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(10)$ given below, compute $P(X=7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0103\\,$ | $\\,0.0293\\,$ | $\\,0.0671\\,$ | $\\,0.1301\\,$ | $\\,0.2202\\,$ | $\\,0.3328\\,$ | $\\,0.4579\\,$ |\n\n$P(X=7)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & =P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\})+P(X=7) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 6)+P(X=7) \\\\  & =F(6)+P(X=7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=7) & =F(7)-F(6) \\\\  & =0.2202-0.1301 \\\\  & =0.0901.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-051c70a8-cf85-5100-9515-597f30cc3693"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-051c70a8-cf85-5100-9515-597f30cc3693" :answer-field/id #uuid "051c70a8-cf85-5100-9515-597f30cc3693" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fba073e2-4b1f-5dc6-b5ca-445184ad40a4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fba073e2-4b1f-5dc6-b5ca-445184ad40a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fba073e2-4b1f-5dc6-b5ca-445184ad40a4" :answer/id #uuid "fba073e2-4b1f-5dc6-b5ca-445184ad40a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0901" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bfd17aa5-30fb-5cb9-aef8-99d3d322cf8d" :question/id #uuid "bfd17aa5-30fb-5cb9-aef8-99d3d322cf8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-225061" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(8)$ given below, compute $P(5<X<9).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0996\\,$ | $\\,0.1912\\,$ | $\\,0.3134\\,$ | $\\,0.4530\\,$ | $\\,0.5925\\,$ | $\\,0.7166\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(8) & =P(X<9) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,8\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\})+P(X\\in \\{6,7,8\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 5)+P(5<X<9) \\\\  & =F(5)+P(5<X<9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5<X<9) & =F(8)-F(5) \\\\  & =0.5925-0.1912 \\\\  & =0.4013.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-67c0c25f-5114-5911-a607-39d35b3593d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-67c0c25f-5114-5911-a607-39d35b3593d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "67c0c25f-5114-5911-a607-39d35b3593d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c7c8c73d-7ec6-551e-abb6-3d12a4c29a22" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c7c8c73d-7ec6-551e-abb6-3d12a4c29a22" "answer-5859446f-1105-516b-a9db-47ed0b0b6da9" "answer-3ae0e9c0-dec1-57ea-83c6-26d6b6f4215e" "answer-6928677a-241c-5b13-8914-64885e8b9340" "answer-4d3e08c2-6ab6-554b-a95c-c2795a89a993"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7c8c73d-7ec6-551e-abb6-3d12a4c29a22" :answer/id #uuid "c7c8c73d-7ec6-551e-abb6-3d12a4c29a22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4013" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5859446f-1105-516b-a9db-47ed0b0b6da9" :answer/id #uuid "5859446f-1105-516b-a9db-47ed0b0b6da9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0