:question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1bd524d5-d969-5fdc-85e1-96731361041c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1bd524d5-d969-5fdc-85e1-96731361041c" :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd524d5-d969-5fdc-85e1-96731361041c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-87766c55-68f3-5682-b6fb-94ccde26296e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-87766c55-68f3-5682-b6fb-94ccde26296e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87766c55-68f3-5682-b6fb-94ccde26296e" :answer/id #uuid "87766c55-68f3-5682-b6fb-94ccde26296e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6594" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167154 :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(5)$ given below, compute $P(X>4).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.1247\\,$ | $\\,0.2650\\,$ | $\\,0.4405\\,$ | $\\,0.6160\\,$ | $\\,0.7622\\,$ | $\\,0.8666\\,$ | $\\,0.9319\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>4) & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-F(4) \\\\  & =1-0.4405 \\\\  & =0.5595.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163974 :answer-field/correct 17592186163978 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-51b5f656-5014-5979-a4cf-5d15629f454f" :question/id #uuid "51b5f656-5014-5979-a4cf-5d15629f454f" :question/math-academy-id "q-225079" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(3)$ given below, compute $P(X>5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0498\\,$ | $\\,0.1991\\,$ | $\\,0.4232\\,$ | $\\,0.6472\\,$ | $\\,0.8153\\,$ | $\\,0.9161\\,$ | $\\,0.9665\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>5) & =1-P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =1-F(5) \\\\  & =1-0.9161 \\\\  & =0.0839.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-416ad32a-01b9-56a7-b237-0306a75530f5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-416ad32a-01b9-56a7-b237-0306a75530f5" :answer-field/id #uuid "416ad32a-01b9-56a7-b237-0306a75530f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2f01f279-b478-5b3b-9f12-398739dfd7da" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4e48dc12-e75f-5206-a9ab-cb83f164828a" "answer-2f01f279-b478-5b3b-9f12-398739dfd7da" "answer-8f5bcdba-d33b-591c-8f35-7033f93c02d4" "answer-49ec3dad-10b2-586c-9514-ba768dab6a50" "answer-f9582ec0-20d1-5343-8057-eff79aa1bf2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e48dc12-e75f-5206-a9ab-cb83f164828a" :answer/id #uuid "4e48dc12-e75f-5206-a9ab-cb83f164828a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0335" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f01f279-b478-5b3b-9f12-398739dfd7da" :answer/id #uuid "2f01f279-b478-5b3b-9f12-398739dfd7da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0839" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f5bcdba-d33b-591c-8f35-7033f93c02d4" :answer/id #uuid "8f5bcdba-d33b-591c-8f35-7033f93c02d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1847" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49ec3dad-10b2-586c-9514-ba768dab6a50" :answer/id #uuid "49ec3dad-10b2-586c-9514-ba768dab6a50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8153" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9582ec0-20d1-5343-8057-eff79aa1bf2d" :answer/id #uuid "f9582ec0-20d1-5343-8057-eff79aa1bf2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9161" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167155 :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(2)$ given below, compute $P(X\\ge 4).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.6767\\,$ | $\\,0.8571\\,$ | $\\,0.9473\\,$ | $\\,0.9834\\,$ | $\\,0.9955\\,$ | $\\,0.9989\\,$ | $\\,0.9998\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 4)=P(X>3).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 4) & =P(X>3) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-F(3) \\\\  & =1-0.8571 \\\\  & =0.1429.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163980 :answer-field/correct 17592186163985 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-9ba81e5b-3639-5408-81fe-d49741329753" :question/id #uuid "9ba81e5b-3639-5408-81fe-d49741329753" :question/math-academy-id "q-225081" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(8)$ given below, compute $P(X>6).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0030\\,$ | $\\,0.0138\\,$ | $\\,0.0424\\,$ | $\\,0.0996\\,$ | $\\,0.1912\\,$ | $\\,0.3134\\,$ | $\\,0.4530\\,$ |\n\n$P(X>6)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6) & =1-P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =1-F(6) \\\\  & =1-0.3134 \\\\  & =0.6866.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1908f630-0728-5a3d-8b69-276311707e74"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1908f630-0728-5a3d-8b69-276311707e74" :answer-field/id #uuid "1908f630-0728-5a3d-8b69-276311707e74" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-61d5f567-d552-53d8-8c2e-4f7d328c39c1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-61d5f567-d552-53d8-8c2e-4f7d328c39c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61d5f567-d552-53d8-8c2e-4f7d328c39c1" :answer/id #uuid "61d5f567-d552-53d8-8c2e-4f7d328c39c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6866" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fcbdd763-0262-5c2f-847d-f89b9e62dad1" :question/id #uuid "fcbdd763-0262-5c2f-847d-f89b9e62dad1" :question/math-academy-id "q-225083" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(7)$ given below, compute $P(X>9).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ | $\\,0.5987\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | $\\,0.8305\\,$ | $\\,0.9015\\,$ | $\\,0.9467\\,$ |\n\n$P(X>9)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>9) & =1-P(X\\le 9) \\\\  & =1-F(9) \\\\  & =1-0.8305 \\\\  & =0.1695.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b06dc7f5-a38d-5157-9f43-316d4d0242b2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b06dc7f5-a38d-5157-9f43-316d4d0242b2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b06dc7f5-a38d-5157-9f43-316d4d0242b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-61550479-df74-5418-86ee-15f4b3056f1f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-61550479-df74-5418-86ee-15f4b3056f1f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61550479-df74-5418-86ee-15f4b3056f1f" :answer/id #uuid "61550479-df74-5418-86ee-15f4b3056f1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1695" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168157 :tutorial/content "When performing certain types of statistical tests (e.g., hypothesis testing), we often need to use standard cumulative distribution function (CDF) tables to carry out the test.\n\nIn this lesson, we'll learn how to construct CDF tables for the Poisson distribution and use them to calculate probabilities.\n\nFirst, recall that the probability mass function of the Poisson distribution $\\textrm{Po}(\\lambda)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{\\lambda^x e^{-\\lambda}}{x!}, \\qquad x=0,1,2,\\ldots\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda$ is a positive parameter.\n\nThe CDF of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's compute the values of $F(x)$ for the distribution $\\textrm{Po}(2)$ at $x=0$ and $x=1.$  \n\nTo do that, we use the definition of the cumulative distribution function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{0}\\cdot {e}^{-2}}{0!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-2}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.1353 \\\\ F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{0}\\cdot {e}^{-2}}{0!}+\\frac{{2}^{1}\\cdot {e}^{-2}}{1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-2}}{1}+\\frac{2\\cdot {e}^{-2}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.4060\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe CDF data is usually presented as a table. If we were to continue this process and calculate $F(2), F(3), F(4),$ and $F(5),$ our table would look as follows:\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $\\cdots$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.1353\\,$ | $\\,0.4060\\,$ | $\\,0.6767\\,$ | $\\,0.8571\\,$ | $\\,0.9473\\,$ | $\\,0.9834\\,$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\cdots\\,\\,\\,$ |\n\nNote the following:\n\n- $F(x)$ is an increasing function.\n\n- Since $\\textrm{Po}(\\lambda)$ takes arbitrarily large values, we have $F(x) < 1$ for all $n,$ and $F(x) \\to 1$ as $x\\to\\infty.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167037 :activity/expected-seconds 540.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
